  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nThe central idea is to develop a hybrid optimization approach that leverages both efficient gradient-based methods and randomized restarts with adaptive resampling. Unlike previous methods that focus purely on gradient descent or binary search, this strategy dynamically balances exploration and exploitation by:\n   - Starting with a high-resolution candidate and progressively relaxing constraints\n   - Using projected gradient descent for local refinement\n   - Incorporating random restarts at multiple resolutions to escape local optima\n   - Adapting hyperparameters between optimization phases based on local gradient information\n\nThe key bottleneck addressed is the tendency of gradient-based methods to get stuck in shallow local optima. By combining these with multi-resolution restarts, we maintain a broad search space while still allowing deep refinement.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n**Representation**:\n- Discrete grid with n_points samples over [0,2]\n- h \u2208 \u211d\u207f, 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1, \u2211h[i] = n_points/2\n\n**Objective**:\nC\u2085 = max\u2096 (1/n_points) \u2211\u1d62 (h[i] * (1-h[i+k]))dx\n- Modes: full correlation with finite support\n- Returns maximum normalized overlap\n\n**Constraints**:\n- Bounded values: 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n- Integral constraint: \u2211h[i] = n_points/2\n\n**Algorithm**:\nAdaptive projected gradient descent with multi-resolution restarts:\n\ndef projected_gradient_step(h, constraint_matrix):\n    while time_remaining(deadline):\n        gradient = compute_correlation_gradient(h)\n        new_h = h - step_size * gradient\n        new_h = project_constraint(new_h)\n        if C\u2085(new_h) < best_c5:\n            best_c5 = C\u2085(new_h)\n            best_h = new_h\n\ndef restart_phase(grid_size, start_h):\n    h = resample(start_h, grid_size)\n    h = project_constraint(h)\n    while time_remaining(deadline) and not_converged:\n        projected_gradient_step(h, grid_size)\n\n**Variables**:\n- Time budget allocation: Phase1=50%, Phase2=30%, Phase3=20%\n- Phase1 (high res): 760 grid points (double initial 380)\n- Phase2 (coarse): 380 grid points\n- Phase3 (final): 1520 grid points\n- Step size adaptation: Exponential decay with local gradient normalization\n- Constraint projection: Dynamic range maintenance (0-1) and sum adjustment\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n**Phase 0: Initialization**\n- Start with initial_h_values (380 grid)\n- Compute initial correlation score\n- Project initial_h_values to satisfy constraint\n\n**Phase 1: Phase1 - Projected Gradient with Higher Resolution**\n- Upsample to 760 grid (dx=2/760)\n- Apply aggressive projected gradient:\n  - Step size = 0.015 * (initial_learning_rate)\n  - Gradient normalization via singular value decomposition\n  - Maximum 2000 iterations unless time exhausted\n- Periodically restart from best candidate (every 500 seconds)\n\n**Step 2: Phase2 - Coarse Grid Verification**\n- Project best candidate back to 380 grid\n- Apply less aggressive gradient descent:\n  - Step size drops 60% per phase3 restart\n  - Run 500 iterations or until plateau\n- Save best candidate from this phase\n\n**Step 3: Phase3 - Final Multi-resolution Polishing**\n- Create three candidates at grid sizes: 380, 760, 1520\n- For each candidate:\n  - Apply constrained gradient descent with smallest step size\n  - Use increasingly aggressive projection if constraints bind\n- Final projection to ensure:\n  0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1\n  \u2211h[i] = grid_size/2\n- Return best candidate across all grids\n\n**Helper Functions**:\ndef project_constraint(h):\n    h_proj = np.clip(h, 0, 1)\n    sum_val = h_proj.sum()\n    if abs(sum_val - grid_size/2) > 1e-4:\n        scale = (grid_size/2) / sum_val\n        h_proj *= scale\n    return h_proj\n\ndef compute_correlation_gradient(h):\n    corr_full = np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')\n    max_index = np.argmax(corr_full)\n    return np.diff(corr_full)[max_index]\n\n**Phase Transitions**:\n- Phase switch when time_remaining < 40 seconds\n- Budget splits: \n  Phase1: 0-50%, Phase2: 50-80%, Phase3: 80-100%\n- Use early termination if plateau detected\n\n4. Search Choices and Variations\n**Parameter Scheduling**:\n- Initial step size: 0.015\n- Decay rate: 0.992 per 100 seconds\n- Grid resolutions: 380, 760, 1520\n\n**Adaptive Strategies**:\n- When constraints bind (h[i] near 0 or 1), \n  increase projection weight by 10%\n- When correlation decreases, \n  reduce learning rate by 15%\n- When correlation stagnates,\n  switch to random resampling at closest grid\n\n**Fallbacks**:\n- If grid projection causes instability,\n  revert to smaller grid\n- If computation time exceeds budget,\n  return best candidate\n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness\n**Dominant Costs**:\n- FFT operations: ~2*N * log(N) per grid\n- Gradient calculation: 15*N operations\n- Upsampling: ~N*log(N) complexity\n\n**Time Estimates**:\n- Phase1 (760 grid): ~450 seconds\n- Phase2 (380 grid): ~300 seconds\n- Phase3 (1520 grid): ~350 seconds\n- Total: 1100 seconds\n\n**Deadline Enforcement**:\n- Check time_remaining at beginning of each phase\n- Early termination if improvement <1e-7 for 5 steps\n- Maintain budget buffer throughout\n\n**Numerical Handling**:\n- Prevent underflow/overflow via clipping\n- Use double precision for gradient calculations\n- Estimate/impute outlier gradients\n\n6. Validation and Return Contract\n**Feasibility Checks**:\n1. Verify 0 \u2264 h[i] \u2264 1 for all i\n2. Confirm \u2211h[i] \u2248 grid_size/2 (tolerance 1e-6)\n3. Recompute C\u2085 with full correlation check\n4. Validate gradient calculation with finite difference test\n\n**Objective Recheck**:\nfinal_c5 = (np.max(np.correlate(h, 1-h, mode='full')) / grid_size) * 2\n\n**Output Contract**:\n- h_values: numpy array of grid size n\n- c5_bound: float (final computed correlation)\n- n_points: grid size (original 380 or upsampled)\n\n**Post-Processing**:\ndef post_validate(h, grid_size):\n    if not np.all((0 <= h[i] <= 1 for i in range(grid_size)) or \n        abs(np.sum(h) - grid_size/2) > 1e-4:\n        return False\n    return True\n\ndef return_candidates(h_list):\n    grid_sizes = [380, 760, 1520]\n    for i, h in enumerate(h_list):\n        if grid_size[i] is not None and not post_validate(h, grid_size[i]):\n            continue\n        c5_val = compute_c5(h, grid_size[i])\n        if c5_val < best_c5:\n            best_c5 = c5_val\n            best_h = h.copy()",
